<section class="solid band"><div class="wrap appph">
  <div>
    <span class="eyebrow rv">On any phone</span>
    <h2 class="rv">Do our web apps work on phones?</h2>
    <p class="sub rv">Yes. A web app opens in the browser, so the same app works on every phone, tablet and computer, and people can add it to their home screen like an app. We build web apps, not App Store or Play Store apps, so there is nothing to download and one version to keep up to date. Looking for app development in Malaysia? A web app is often the quicker way to reach every phone.</p>
    <ul class="ticks rv"><li>Layouts that fit small screens</li><li>Light pages that load quickly on phones</li><li>Charts and tables that fit the screen</li><li>Logins and payments that work on a phone</li></ul>
  </div>
  <img class="rv" src="/img/fs-phone-home.webp" srcset="/img/fs-phone-home-360.webp 360w, /img/fs-phone-home.webp 640w" sizes="(max-width: 900px) 240px, 300px" width="640" height="1322" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="XpertForesight Research home on a phone: pick a search, type a keyword and choose the country, with the research tools below" />
</div></section>

<section id="payments" class="dark band"><div class="wrap split">
  <div>
    <span class="eyebrow rv">Payment gateway integration</span>
    <h2 class="rv">Which payment gateway do we set up?</h2>
    <p class="sub rv">Stripe. When people look for a payment gateway in Malaysia, they need two things: a provider, and someone to connect it properly to their website. Stripe is the provider; we do the payment gateway integration. Your customers pay on Stripe's own secure payment page by card, FPX online banking or GrabPay, and it is the same set up seoxpert.my uses to take payments. Ask us about other gateways.</p>
    <p class="sub rv">Comparing providers first? Read our <a href="/blog/payment-gateway-malaysia/">guide to payment gateways in Malaysia</a>, with the published fees for cards, FPX and e-wallets.</p>
    <p class="rv"><a class="btn" href="/contact/" data-track="get-a-quote">Get a quote</a></p>
  </div>
  <ul class="applist">
    <li class="rv"><b>One-time payments</b>A fixed price for a product, a service or a booking.</li>
    <li class="rv" style="--d:1"><b>Subscriptions</b>Monthly or yearly plans that renew by themselves.</li>
    <li class="rv" style="--d:2"><b>Payment links</b>A link you can send in a message, with no page to build.</li>
    <li class="rv" style="--d:3"><b>Card, FPX and GrabPay</b>The ways people in Malaysia like to pay, on one page.</li>
    <li class="rv"><b>Access after payment</b>Stripe tells your web app the moment a payment goes through, and access unlocks.</li>
    <li class="rv" style="--d:1"><b>Receipts by email</b>Stripe emails every customer a receipt.</li>
    <li class="rv" style="--d:2"><b>Billing portal</b>Customers change their card or plan, or cancel, by themselves.</li>
    <li class="rv" style="--d:3"><b>Card details stay with Stripe</b>Payments happen on Stripe's own page, never on your server.</li>
  </ul>
</div></section>

<section class="solid tint band"><div class="wrap split">
  <div class="stick">
    <span class="eyebrow rv">How we build</span>
    <h2 class="rv">How do we build web apps?</h2>
    <p class="sub rv">The same way we build XpertInsight and XpertForesight, and the same way this website is built. See every layer of <a href="/website-development/#secure">secure by design</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <ol class="nsteps">
    <li class="rv"><h3>Fast static pages for the public part</h3><p>Everything anyone can see is real text in fast pages, so it can be found on Google and in AI search.</p></li>
    <li class="rv" style="--d:1"><h3>Server functions on a global cloud network</h3><p>Logins, payments and data run in small server functions on a global cloud network, close to your users.</p></li>
    <li class="rv" style="--d:2"><h3>Secrets stay on the server</h3><p>Keys, prices and the checks that matter live on the server, never in the browser where anyone could read them.</p></li>
    <li class="rv" style="--d:3"><h3>One-time-code logins</h3><p>A fresh code by email each time, so there are no passwords to store, guess or leak.</p></li>
    <li class="rv" style="--d:4"><h3>Every version kept</h3><p>Every change is saved, so an earlier version can be put back quickly if something goes wrong.</p></li>
  </ol>
</div></section>

<section class="solid band"><div class="wrap split">
  <div class="stick">
    <span class="eyebrow rv">How it starts</span>
    <h2 class="rv">How does a web app project work?</h2>
    <p class="sub rv">Every web app is different, so there is no package price. Here is how we get from your idea to a quote and a plan. For a regular business website, see our <a href="/website-development/">website development packages</a>.</p>
  </div>
  <ol class="nsteps">
    <li class="rv"><h3>Tell us what it should do</h3><p>Who will use it, what they need to see or do, and how people should pay. A short message on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> is enough to begin.</p></li>
    <li class="rv" style="--d:1"><h3>We agree the scope, the plan and the dates</h3><p>We write down what will be built and the dates for each step, then send a quote based on that scope. Nothing starts until you agree.</p></li>
    <li class="rv" style="--d:2"><h3>We build it in steps</h3><p>You check each step before it goes live, so there are no surprises at the end.</p></li>
    <li class="rv" style="--d:3"><h3>Launch, then keep it healthy</h3><p>Your web app goes live with its public pages ready for Google and AI search. <a href="/seo-services-malaysia/">XpertRank, our expert SEO service,</a> can help those pages grow.</p></li>
  </ol>
</div></section>

